Hi Longsi,

If you take a look of the intensity distribution of the raw data, you can
find the majority of the data is very low expresse while some probes are
very highly expressed. The log2 or vst (variance stabilizing transform)
transform is to suppress this dynamic range of intensity and make the
normalization, especially the curve-fitting related normalization, easier to
perform. If the normalization algorithm can deal with the raw data (with
wide dynamic range of intensity) well, it should have no big difference of
the order.


Pan


