On a 32 bit machine, a single process cannot use more than x GB (with  
x depending a bit on the OS, but typically something like 2-3 GB), so  
the huge swap does not help you at all.

You might want to look for aroma.affymetrix when Henrik Bengstsson  
gets around to releasing that (in August he says). That will also  
help you process an unlimited number of snp arrays in bounded memory  
(typically something like 500mb). Of course, only certain algorithms  
are implemented in that package.

